  "node": {
    "id": "ctkg:v3e-object-a87ce6bc6021170d799c3280",
    "canonicalType": "KnowledgeStatement",
    "label": "与不考虑原有开环零极点位置而任意指定所有极点的方案相比，一种仅旨在改善开环响应中不理想特性、同时避免带宽大幅增加或避免移动靠近零点的极点的极点配置设计思想，通常允许采用较小的增益，从而可以使用较小功率的控制执行机构。",
    "aliases": [],
    "description": "A pole-placement philosophy that aims to fix only the undesirable aspects of the open-loop response and avoids either large increases in bandwidth or efforts to move poles that are near zeros will typically allow smaller gains, and thus smaller control actuators, than a philosophy that arbitrarily picks all the poles without regard to the original open-loop pole and zero locations.",
